  {
    "text": "1. Ask About the Right Things",
    "url": "https://www.nngroup.com/articles/survey-best-practices/?lm=should-you-run-a-survey&pt=article#toc-1-ask-about-the-right-things-1"
  },
  {
    "text": "2. Use Language that Is Neutral, Natural, and Clear",
    "url": "https://www.nngroup.com/articles/survey-best-practices/?lm=should-you-run-a-survey&pt=article#toc-2-use-language-that-is-neutral-natural-and-clear-2"
  },
  {
    "text": "3. Don\u2019t Ask Respondents to Predict Behavior",
    "url": "https://www.nngroup.com/articles/survey-best-practices/?lm=should-you-run-a-survey&pt=article#toc-3-dont-ask-respondents-to-predict-behavior-3"
  },
  {
    "text": "4. Focus on Closed-Ended Questions",
    "url": "https://www.nngroup.com/articles/survey-best-practices/?lm=should-you-run-a-survey&pt=article#toc-4-focus-on-closed-ended-questions-4"
  },
  {
    "text": "5. Avoid Double-Barreled Questions",
    "url": "https://www.nngroup.com/articles/survey-best-practices/?lm=should-you-run-a-survey&pt=article#toc-5-avoid-double-barreled-questions-5"
  },
  {
    "text": "6. Use Balanced Scales",
    "url": "https://www.nngroup.com/articles/survey-best-practices/?lm=should-you-run-a-survey&pt=article#toc-6-use-balanced-scales-6"
  },
  {
    "text": "7. Answer Options Should Be All-Inclusive and Mutually Exclusive",
    "url": "https://www.nngroup.com/articles/survey-best-practices/?lm=should-you-run-a-survey&pt=article#toc-7-answer-options-should-be-all-inclusive-and-mutually-exclusive-7"
  },
  {
    "text": "8. Provide an Opt-Out",
    "url": "https://www.nngroup.com/articles/survey-best-practices/?lm=should-you-run-a-survey&pt=article#toc-8-provide-an-opt-out-8"
  },
  {
    "text": "9. Allow Most Questions to Be Optional",
    "url": "https://www.nngroup.com/articles/survey-best-practices/?lm=should-you-run-a-survey&pt=article#toc-9-allow-most-questions-to-be-optional-9"
  },
